jectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Consonant Clusters: th and nt"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Consonant clusters are groups of two consonants or more together. They form a specific sound when they are combined in a particular way. Usually the sounds of some of the consonants may be reduced or dropped. <br/><br/> In -th consonant clusters, the /th/ sound can be changed or dropped to sound more like a /t/ sound. In the plural form of words ending in th, the final sound can be /s/ or /z/. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">months = /mons/</span><br/><br/>In -nt consonant clusters, the /t/ sound can be dropped if it is followed by a vowel sound. In that case, a flapped /n/ is used in its place.<span class=\"strong\"><br/>Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">center = /cen'ner/ or </span><span class=\"italic\">twenty = /twen'ny/</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading the following sentences aloud:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Often adding a layered program give your loyalty program <span class=\"strong\">depth</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The goal is to create a program that will capture your guests' attention and motivate <span class=\"strong\">incremental </span>spending over a long period of time. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The core loyalty program you select should enable promotions that <span class=\"strong\">accentuate</span> your restaurant. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Intonation in Lists"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about lists, it is important to use the right stress and intonation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When naming items in a list, you use rising intonation for the first item in the list and falling intonation for the last. Falling intonation indicates the end of the list."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <span class=\"italic\">It defines the program's rewards and how they are \u2197<span class=\"strong\">earned</span>, \u2197<span class=\"strong\">redeemed</span>, and \u2198<span class=\"strong\">expired</span>. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the following sentences from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Three common elements make up every loyalty program: <span class=\"strong\">the core program</span>, <span class=\"strong\">layered programs</span> and <span class=\"strong\">promotions</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": " They emphasize your restaurant's' <span class=\"strong\">distinctive</span> character in a way that <span class=\"strong\">appeals to guests</span>, <span class=\"strong\">motivates them to visit more often</span> and <span class=\"strong\">to spend more of their dining dollars with you<span class=\"strong\">."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It defines the program's rewards and how they are <span class=\"strong\">earned</span>, <span class=\"strong\">redeemed</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">expired</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Targeted promotions can help <span class=\"strong\">generate traffic during slow periods or specific parts of the day</span>, <span class=\"strong\">encourage the trial of new menu items</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">keep your restaurants on the minds of your guests</span>."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "distinctive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a special quality, character, or appearance that is different and easy to recognize"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They should emphasize your restaurant's' distinctive character."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about loyalty p